===Declined candidates===
*[[Manuel Baldizón]]: deputy of the Congress 2004-2008, secretary-general of [[Renewed Democratic Liberty]] 2010-2014, presidential candidate in 2011 and 2015.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.soy502.com/articulo/baldizon-confirma-no-buscara-presidencia-30612 |title=Manuel Baldizón confirma que ya no buscará la Presidencia |newspaper=Soy502|date=24 July 2017}}</ref>
*Ernest Steve "Neto" Bran: Mayor of [[Mixco]] since 2016.<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://diariodigital.gt/2016/09/alvaro-arzu-el-ejemplo-a-seguir-de-neto-bran/ |title=Álvaro Arzú, el ejemplo a seguir de Neto Bran |newspaper=Diario Digital |date=16 September 2016 |access-date=21 February 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170729050525/http://diariodigital.gt/2016/09/alvaro-arzu-el-ejemplo-a-seguir-de-neto-bran/ |archive-date=29 July 2017 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.prensalibre.com/ciudades/guatemala/neto-bran-sigue-los-pasos-de-arzu-aseguran-expertos|title=Neto Bran sigue los pasos de Arzú, aseguran expertos|date=24 November 2017}}</ref>
*[[Jorge Pérez (politician)|Jorge Pérez]]: Secretary of Executive Coordination of the Presidency 2000-2002.<ref name=candidates/>
*[[Erik Súñiga]]: [[Mayor|Mayor of]] [[Ayutla, San Marcos]], 2008-2020.<ref name=candidates/>
*[[Nineth Montenegro]]: [[Congress of Guatemala|Deputy of the Congress]] by National List since 1996, [[Congress of Guatemala|Second Vice President of the Congress]] 2012-2013, General Secretary of the Encuentro de Guatemala since 2007.

